    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d393">

                <pb facs="d392-3" n="3" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve10/pgd392-3"/>

                <head>393. Telegram 814 From the Embassy in Haiti to the Department of State<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d393-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d393-f2"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Port-au-Prince</placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1970-07-01T20:05:00+00:00">July 1,
                            1970, 2005Z</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <pb facs="d393-1" n="1" xml:id="pgd393-1"/>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subject:</label>
                    <item>Alleged Subversive Activities in US Against Haiti</item>
                </list>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>Ref:</head>
                    <item>Port au Prince 786</item>
                </list>
                <p>1. Have just received formal note from Under Secretary Raymond expatiating on our
                    conversation of June 24.</p>
                <p>2. Note declares group of “so-called political exiles organizing on US territory
                    to carry out acts international brigandage against Haiti.” It names leaders this
                    group as Rene Leon, Robert Basile, Octave Cayard, Daniel Beauvoir, Francois
                    benoit, fritz germain, henry vixamar, father jean-baptiste georges, luc fouche,
                    and marcel fombrun. note also affirms they trying obtain aircraft to bomb haiti
                    and are already in possession of boat, which kept near miami, to be used in
                    landing commandos in haiti.</p>
                <p>3. In penultimate paragraph, note calls attention to fact that such activities in
                    violation neutrality act, contrary to international law, dangerous to
                    hemispheric peace, and favorable to advancement Marxist-Leninist cause in Haiti.
                    It also recalls action taken recently against Alpha 66 group and asks USG “take necessary measures prevent these terrorists
                    from realizing their criminal intentions against Haiti.”</p>
                <pb facs="d393-2" n="2" xml:id="pgd393-2"/>
                <p>4. In view this further demarche by GOH, repeat
                    request made in reftel that Dept furnish any
                    information available to it on activities this group.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Knox</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d393-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d393-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Files 1970–73, POL 23–9 HAI. Confidential.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d393-f2" n="2" xml:id="d393-f2-content">
                <p>Ambassador Knox reported that the
                    Government of Haiti had delivered a formal note calling on the U.S. Government
                    to take action against Haitian exiles, who were allegedly preparing to attack
                    Haiti from the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
